---
// Way 2: building presence and connection one on one.
// Skills, assignments and the email guide come from src/data/course.ts
// through WayPage; the copy and steps on this page live here.
import WayPage from '../../components/WayPage.astro';
import Photo from '../../components/Photo.astro';

const routine = [
  ['Greet', 'Walk up, say hello, and give your name.', 'Hi, I’m Max.'],
  ['Ask', 'Ask a question about them.', 'How did you end up in the fintech club?'],
  ['Listen', 'Let them finish. Do not plan your next line while they talk.', ''],
  ['Paraphrase', 'Say back what you heard.', 'So you joined for the competition, and stayed for the people.'],
];
const pitch = [
  ['Who you are', 'I’m Max, a business student at SMU.'],
  ['Your focus', 'I’m digging into how AI is changing financial decisions.'],
  ['Your proof', 'This summer I built a model that matched weather data to restaurant sales.'],
  ['Hand it back', 'What are you working on right now?'],
];
const listeners = [
  ['A potential boss', 'Lead with your proof and what you can do for their team.', 'Ask what the team is working on, and what they look for in an intern.'],
  ['A useful connection', 'Lead with your focus, and why their work interests you.', 'Ask about their path, and who else you should meet.'],
  ['A classmate or peer', 'Lead with what you are curious about right now.', 'Ask what they are working on, and whether you could work on something together.'],
];
const answer = [
  ['Thesis', 'Answer the question in one sentence.', 'I’m good at turning messy data into a decision someone can act on.'],
  ['Preview', 'Say how many examples are coming.', 'Two examples come to mind.'],
  ['Example one', 'Tell it, then say what it shows.', 'At my summer internship, I... That shows I can...'],
  ['Example two', 'Tell it, then say what it shows.', 'For my weather and restaurant project, I... That shows I can...'],
  ['Restate', 'Say the thesis again.', 'So that’s how I work: messy data in, clear decision out.'],
  ['Stop', 'Stop talking. Let them ask the next question.', ''],
];
---
<WayPage i={1}>
  <div slot="about" class="grid content-center gap-6 rounded-[28px] bg-foreground px-6 py-10 text-background sm:px-10">
    <p class="font-serif text-3xl leading-[1.12] tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-4xl">
      One on one, connection means the other person feels heard before they hear about you.
    </p>
    <div class="grid content-start gap-3 leading-relaxed text-background/70">
      <p>You do not need to be charismatic. You need a routine you can repeat: open a conversation, say who you are in a minute, and answer hard questions with the same structure you use for speeches.</p>
      <p>The three steps below build on each other, from meeting someone to interviewing with them.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section slot="steps" class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 data-reveal class="h-section">The steps</h2>

      <div class="mt-10 grid items-center gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
      <h3 data-reveal class="h-sub">1. Open a conversation: greet, ask, listen, paraphrase</h3>
      <p class="max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Do all four, in order, before you say anything about yourself.</p>
        </div>
        <Photo name="step-greet" alt="A young professional shaking hands across a table" />
      </div>
      <ol data-reveal class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        {routine.map(([name, text, line], k) => (
          <li class="rounded-[18px] border bg-card p-5">
            <span class="font-serif text-2xl leading-none text-primary">{k + 1}</span>
            <p class="mt-2 font-semibold">{name}</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">{text}</p>
            {line && <p class="mt-3 border-l-2 border-primary/40 pl-3 text-sm italic">“{line}”</p>}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>

      <div class="mt-14 grid items-center gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
      <h3 data-reveal class="h-sub">2. Say who you are: the 60-second elevator pitch</h3>
      <p class="max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Your pitch is your LinkedIn hook, said out loud. Use it when someone asks what you do.</p>
        </div>
        <Photo name="step-pitch" alt="A young man introducing himself at a networking event" />
      </div>
      <ol data-reveal class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        {pitch.map(([name, line], k) => (
          <li class="rounded-[18px] border bg-card p-5">
            <span class="font-serif text-2xl leading-none text-primary">{k + 1}</span>
            <p class="mt-2 font-semibold">{name}</p>
            <p class="mt-3 border-l-2 border-primary/40 pl-3 text-sm italic">“{line}”</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-6 font-semibold">Same four parts every time. Only the emphasis changes:</p>
      <div data-reveal class="mt-3 grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-3">
        {listeners.map(([who, lead, ask]) => (
          <div class="rounded-[18px] bg-secondary/60 p-5">
            <p class="font-serif text-2xl leading-tight">{who}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">{lead}</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">{ask}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14 grid items-center gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
      <h3 data-reveal class="h-sub">3. Answer interview questions: modified macro structure</h3>
      <p class="max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">An interview answer is a short speech you did not get to prepare. Use the same skeleton, shrunk down. Sample question: “Tell me about a time you solved a problem.”</p>
        </div>
        <Photo name="step-interview" alt="Two young men shaking hands at the end of an interview" />
      </div>
      <ol data-reveal class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {answer.map(([name, text, line], k) => (
          <li class="rounded-[18px] border bg-card p-5">
            <span class="font-serif text-2xl leading-none text-primary">{k + 1}</span>
            <p class="mt-2 font-semibold">{name}</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">{text}</p>
            {line && <p class="mt-3 border-l-2 border-primary/40 pl-3 text-sm italic">“{line}”</p>}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted-foreground">Pick your example before you start explaining it. Thinking of a better one halfway through and backing up to set it up is how answers fall apart.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</WayPage>
